# Nested pages, then ecommerce, then the post, then Zenodo

MCP is not a product. It serves the Payload ecommerce catalogue.

- Nested pages generate every product and every variant, parents first, three deep.
- Ecommerce reads those pages. A product is a depth-2 page. A variant is a depth-3 page under it.
- Each variant is one published blog post.
- Each post is a Zenodo publication through the Payload deposit hooks. The handler does not fetch and does not write.
- Deploy is a Payload hook. The live site tests are the e2e gate after that deploy.
